# DID ANYBODY LOOK FOR COUPLINGS BETWEEN THIS STACK'S LAYERS? One row per filing that was asked,
# carrying what it answered and the note that argues for the answer.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ A STACK WITH NO COUPLINGS FILED HAS EITHER INDEPENDENT LAYERS OR NOBODY WHO LOOKED, and
#    an empty coupling table renders those two identically. They are opposite claims: one
#    licenses treating each remainder on its own, the other says nothing at all. This is where
#    the difference lives.
#
# ⛔ A NULL `answer` IS NOT AN ABSENCE. It means the document filed real couplings, so the
#   search question is answered by the content rather than by a reason.
#
# ⭐⭐ IT WAS HALF OF A UNION THAT FIVE CALLERS TOOK BACK APART. epistemics/searches.sqlc built
#    the two search kinds into one relation with a `looked_for` string, and then every caller
#    that wanted one of them filtered on that string -- entries/coupling_presence.sqlc,
#    reports/independence_tested.sqlc, and two relations that gave up and read pm.coupling_search
#    raw. A union whose members were never files is a union nobody can compose half of.
-- pm:Stack/pm:Couplings/pm:Absent, one row per filing asked.
SELECT cs.filing, cs.absent AS answer, cs.note
FROM pm.coupling_search cs
